Well, I've finally had a chance to update my snapshot of Netty -- and pull in the fixes for issue https://github.com/netty/netty/issues/993, however trying to DECOMPRESS the data with snappy fails.

If I tweak the SnappyFramedDecoder (changing line 98) to the following, it will try to decompress, but will fail the checksum. [Line 98](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/master/codec/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/compression/SnappyFramedDecoder.java#L98)

```
 if (chunkLength == 0 || (chunkType != ChunkType.COMPRESSED_DATA && in.readableBytes() < chunkLength)) {
```

By the way, in line [SnappyFramedDecoder:98](https://github.com/netty/netty/blob/master/codec/src/main/java/io/netty/handler/codec/compression/SnappyFramedDecoder.java#L98), shouldn't it check to see if the data is compressed? Otherwise, it's looking at (in this example) a uncompressed chunk length of 274, but the input stream only has 171 bytes of data (as it's compressed), so it fails, thinking there should be more data when there shouldn't.

Here's my test case:

